====================================================
Problem before: If an API request needs data from multiple services, we may start several asynchronous tasks and handle their failures and cancellation separately.

Conceptually, the work might look like this:

// Conceptual example — not a complete API implementation
var userTask = fetchUserAsync();
var orderTask = fetchOrdersAsync();

// We must coordinate results, errors and cancellation.

Structured concurrency provides an API for treating related concurrent tasks as one unit of work. The exact API syntax has evolved through preview releases.

Why useful?

Coordinate related tasks.

Handle failures and cancellation together.

Make concurrent code easier to reason about.

Interview answer: “Structured Concurrency treats related concurrent tasks as a single unit, improving error handling, cancellation and observability.”

