9. Stable Values — Preview in Java 25
==========================================
Problem before: A final field cannot be reassigned after initialization, but sometimes we want a value to be initialized later while still treating it as stable once initialized.

Traditional example:

private final String appName = "MyApplication";

Java 25 previewed a Stable Values API intended to support values that are initialized later but remain stable after initialization.

Why useful? It aims to give the JVM more opportunities to optimize stable values while allowing more flexible initialization.

Interview answer: “Stable Values were previewed in Java 25 to support values that can be initialized later but remain stable, potentially enabling JVM optimizations.”

This was a preview API. It is an advanced JVM topic, so understand the purpose before studying its API details. 
