10. Java Flight Recorder (JFR) Improvements
============================================
Java 25 also includes improvements to monitoring and performance diagnostics.

JFR Method Timing & Tracing: Adds capabilities for collecting method timing and tracing information.

JFR Cooperative Sampling: Improves the stability of thread-stack sampling.

JFR CPU-Time Profiling: Introduces experimental CPU-time profiling improvements on Linux.

A simplified way to start an application with JFR recording is:

java -XX:StartFlightRecording=filename=app.jfr MyApplication

You can then inspect the recording with Java Flight Recorder tooling to investigate performance problems.

Why useful? These tools help diagnose slow methods, CPU usage and runtime behavior in production applications.

Interview answer: “Java 25 enhances Java Flight Recorder with additional profiling and tracing capabilities to help diagnose application performance issues.” 
